{"id":"mahabharata-3-296","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":296,"title":"षण्णवत्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 296 · The brothers die at the lake","summary":{"en":"Nakula finds a clear lake, but a voice from the sky forbids him to drink until he has answered its questions; ignoring it, he drinks and falls dead, and Sahadeva, Arjuna and Bhima follow and meet the same fate. At last Yudhishthira comes, grieving, finds his brothers lying dead, and hears the voice of a Yaksha.","kn":"ನಕುಲನು ತಿಳಿನೀರಿನ ಸರೋವರ ಕಾಣುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಆದರೆ ಪ್ರಶ್ನೆಗಳಿಗೆ ಉತ್ತರಿಸುವವರೆಗೆ ಕುಡಿಯಬೇಡ ಎಂದು ಆಕಾಶವಾಣಿ ತಡೆಯುತ್ತದೆ; ಕಡೆಗಣಿಸಿ ಕುಡಿದು ಸತ್ತು ಬೀಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಸಹದೇವ, ಅರ್ಜುನ, ಭೀಮರೂ ಅದೇ ಗತಿ ಹೊಂದುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಕೊನೆಗೆ ದುಃಖಿತ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನು ಬಂದು ಸಹೋದರರು ಸತ್ತು ಬಿದ್ದಿರುವುದನ್ನು ಕಂಡು ಯಕ್ಷನ ವಾಣಿಯನ್ನು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"नकुल एक निर्मल सरोवर पाते हैं, पर आकाशवाणी उन्हें प्रश्नों का उत्तर दिए बिना जल पीने से रोकती है; अनसुना कर वे जल पीते हैं और मृत होकर गिर पड़ते हैं, और सहदेव, अर्जुन और भीम भी आकर वही गति पाते हैं। अन्त में शोकाकुल युधिष्ठिर आते हैं, भाइयों को मृत पड़ा पाते हैं और एक यक्ष की वाणी सुनते हैं।","te":"నకులుడు స్వచ్ఛమైన సరస్సును కనుగొంటాడు, కానీ ప్రశ్నలకు బదులిచ్చే వరకు తాగవద్దని ఆకాశవాణి అడ్డుకుంటుంది; పట్టించుకోక తాగి మరణించి పడిపోతాడు; సహదేవుడు, అర్జునుడు, భీముడు కూడా వచ్చి అదే గతి పొందుతారు. చివరకు దుఃఖంతో యుధిష్ఠిరుడు వచ్చి సోదరులు మరణించి పడి ఉండడం చూసి యక్షుని వాణి వింటాడు.","ta":"நகுலன் ஒரு தெளிந்த ஏரியைக் காண்கிறான்; ஆனால் கேள்விகளுக்கு விடையளிக்கும் வரை குடிக்கக் கூடாது என்று வானிலிருந்து ஒரு குரல் தடுக்கிறது; பொருட்படுத்தாமல் குடித்து இறந்து விழ, ஸஹதேவன், அர்ஜுனன், பீமனும் வந்து அதே கதியை அடைகிறார்கள். இறுதியில் துயருற்ற யுதிஷ்டிரர் வந்து சகோதரர்கள் இறந்து கிடப்பதைக் கண்டு ஒரு யக்ஷனின் குரலைக் கேட்கிறார்.","ml":"നകുലൻ തെളിഞ്ഞ ഒരു തടാകം കണ്ടെത്തുന്നു; പക്ഷേ അതിലെ ചോദ്യങ്ങൾക്ക് ഉത്തരം നൽകുംവരെ കുടിക്കരുതെന്ന് ആകാശത്തുനിന്ന് ഒരു ശബ്ദം വിലക്കുന്നു; അതിനെ അവഗണിച്ച് അദ്ദേഹം കുടിച്ചു മരിച്ചുവീഴുന്നു. സഹദേവനും അർജുനനും ഭീമനും പിന്നാലെ വന്ന് അതേ വിധി നേരിടുന്നു. ഒടുവിൽ വിലപിച്ചുകൊണ്ട് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ എത്തുന്നു; സഹോദരന്മാർ മരിച്ചുകിടക്കുന്നത് കാണുന്നു, ഒരു യക്ഷന്റെ ശബ്ദം കേൾക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.296; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"आरणेयपर्व","titleEn":"Araneya Parva (The fire-drill)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"नापदामस्ति मर्यादा न निमित्तं न कारणम् ।\nधर्मस्तु विभजत्यत्र उभयोः पुण्यपापयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For misfortunes there is no limit, no pretext and no reason; it is dharma alone that apportions the merit and the sin of both sides."}},{"text":"भीम उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhima said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"प्रातिकाम्यनयत्कृष्णां सभायां प्रेष्यवत्तदा ।\nन मया निहतस्तत्र तेन प्राप्ताः स्म संशयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pratikamin dragged Krishna into the assembly like a servant, and I did not kill him there; therefore we have met this trouble."}},{"text":"अर्जुन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"वाचस्तीक्ष्णास्थिभेदिन्यः सूतपुत्रेण भाषिताः ।\nअतितीक्ष्णा मया क्षान्तास्तेन प्राप्ताः स्म संशयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sharp words that pierce the bone, spoken by the charioteer's son, were too cutting, and I endured them; therefore we have met this trouble."}},{"text":"सहदेव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sahadeva said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"शकुनिस्त्वां यदाजैषीदक्षद्यूतेन भारत ।\nस मया न हतस्तत्र तेन प्राप्ताः स्म संशयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Shakuni defeated you at dice, Bharata, I did not kill him there; therefore we have met this trouble."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"ततो युधिष्ठिरो राजा नकुलं वाक्यमब्रवीत् ।\nआरुह्य वृक्षं माद्रेय निरीक्षस्व दिशो दश ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Yudhishthira said to Nakula: Climb a tree, son of Madri, and look in all ten directions."}},{"n":6,"text":"पानीयमन्तिके पश्य वृक्षान्वाप्युदकाश्रयान् ।\nइमे हि भ्रातरः श्रान्तास्तव तात पिपासिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"See whether there is water nearby, or trees that grow near water; your brothers here are tired and thirsty, dear one."}},{"n":7,"text":"नकुलस्तु तथेत्युक्त्वा शीघ्रमारुह्य पादपम् ।\nअब्रवीद्भ्रातरं ज्येष्ठमभिवीक्ष्य समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nakula said, So be it, quickly climbed a tree, looked all around, and said to his eldest brother:"}},{"n":8,"text":"पश्यामि बहुलान्राजन्वृक्षानुदकसंश्रयान् ।\nसारसानां च निर्ह्रादमत्रोदकमसंशयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I see many trees that grow near water, king, and the cries of cranes; surely there is water here."}},{"n":9,"text":"ततोऽब्रवीत्सत्यधृतिः कुन्तीपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nगच्छ सौम्य ततः शीघ्रं तूर्णं पानीयमानय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Yudhishthira son of Kunti, firm in truth, said: Go there quickly, gentle one, and bring water at once."}},{"n":10,"text":"नकुलस्तु तथेत्युक्त्वा भ्रातुर्ज्येष्ठस्य शासनात् ।\nप्राद्रवद्यत्र पानीयं शीघ्रं चैवान्वपद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nakula, saying So be it at his eldest brother's command, ran to where the water was and quickly reached it."}},{"n":11,"text":"स दृष्ट्वा विमलं तोयं सारसैः परिवारितम् ।\nपातुकामस्ततो वाचमन्तरिक्षात्स शुश्रुवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing clear water surrounded by cranes, he wanted to drink, and then he heard a voice from the sky."}},{"n":12,"text":"मा तात साहसं कार्षीर्मम पूर्वपरिग्रहः ।\nप्रश्नानुक्त्वा तु माद्रेय ततः पिब हरस्व च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Do not act rashly, dear child; this is my prior possession. Answer my questions first, son of Madri, and then drink and take water."}},{"n":13,"text":"अनादृत्य तु तद्वाक्यं नकुलः सुपिपासितः ।\nअपिबच्छीतलं तोयं पीत्वा च निपपात ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Nakula, very thirsty, disregarded those words, drank the cool water, and having drunk, he fell down."}},{"n":14,"text":"चिरायमाणे नकुले कुन्तीपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nअब्रवीद्भ्रातरं वीरं सहदेवमरिंदमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Nakula was slow to return, Yudhishthira son of Kunti said to his brother, the hero Sahadeva, subduer of foes:"}},{"n":15,"text":"भ्राता चिरायते तात सहदेव तवाग्रजः ।\nतं चैवानय सोदर्यं पानीयं च त्वमानय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dear Sahadeva, your elder brother is late; bring him back, your brother of the same womb, and bring water too."}},{"n":16,"text":"सहदेवस्तथेत्युक्त्वा तां दिशं प्रत्यपद्यत ।\nददर्श च हतं भूमौ भ्रातरं नकुलं तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sahadeva said, So be it, and went in that direction, and there he saw his brother Nakula lying dead on the ground."}},{"n":17,"text":"भ्रातृशोकाभिसंतप्तस्तृषया च प्रपीडितः ।\nअभिदुद्राव पानीयं ततो वागभ्यभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Burning with grief for his brother and oppressed by thirst, he ran to the water, and then a voice spoke to him:"}},{"n":18,"text":"मा तात साहसं कार्षीर्मम पूर्वपरिग्रहः ।\nप्रश्नानुक्त्वा यथाकामं ततः पिब हरस्व च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Do not act rashly, dear child; this is my prior possession. Answer my questions as you please, and then drink and take water."}},{"n":19,"text":"अनादृत्य तु तद्वाक्यं सहदेवः पिपासितः ।\nअपिबच्छीतलं तोयं पीत्वा च निपपात ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Sahadeva, thirsty, disregarded those words, drank the cool water, and having drunk, he fell down."}},{"n":20,"text":"अथाब्रवीत्स विजयं कुन्तीपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nभ्रातरौ ते चिरगतौ बीभत्सो शत्रुकर्शन ।\nतौ चैवानय भद्रं ते पानीयं च त्वमानय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Yudhishthira son of Kunti said to Vijaya: Your two brothers have been gone long, Bibhatsu, tormentor of foes. Good fortune to you; bring them back and bring water too."}},{"n":21,"text":"एवमुक्तो गुडाकेशः प्रगृह्य सशरं धनुः ।\nआमुक्तखड्गो मेधावी तत्सरः प्रत्यपद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus told, the wise Gudakesha took up his bow with arrows, girded his sword, and went to that lake."}},{"n":22,"text":"यतः पुरुषशार्दूलौ पानीयहरणे गतौ ।\nतौ ददर्श हतौ तत्र भ्रातरौ श्वेतवाहनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, where those two tigers among men had gone to fetch water, the white-horsed Arjuna saw his two brothers lying dead."}},{"n":23,"text":"प्रसुप्ताविव तौ दृष्ट्वा नरसिंहः सुदुःखितः ।\nधनुरुद्यम्य कौन्तेयो व्यलोकयत तद्वनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing them as if asleep, the lion among men was deeply pained; the son of Kunti raised his bow and looked around that forest."}},{"n":24,"text":"नापश्यत्तत्र किंचित्स भूतं तस्मिन्महावने ।\nसव्यसाची ततः श्रान्तः पानीयं सोऽभ्यधावत ॥","meaning":{"en":"He saw no creature in that great forest; then Savyasachin, weary, ran to the water."}},{"n":25,"text":"अभिधावंस्ततो वाचमन्तरिक्षात्स शुश्रुवे ।\nकिमासीदसि पानीयं नैतच्छक्यं बलात्त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he ran, he heard a voice from the sky: Why do you hurry to the water? You cannot take it by force."}},{"n":26,"text":"कौन्तेय यदि वै प्रश्नान्मयोक्तान्प्रतिपत्स्यसे ।\nततः पास्यसि पानीयं हरिष्यसि च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Son of Kunti, if you answer the questions I ask, then you may drink the water and take it, Bharata."}},{"n":27,"text":"वारितस्त्वब्रवीत्पार्थो दृश्यमानो निवारय ।\nयावद्बाणैर्विनिर्भिन्नः पुनर्नैवं वदिष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Forbidden, Partha said: Show yourself and stop me, until you are pierced by my arrows and never speak so again."}},{"n":28,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा ततः पार्थः शरैरस्त्रानुमन्त्रितैः ।\nववर्ष तां दिशं कृत्स्नां शब्दवेधं च दर्शयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So saying, Partha rained arrows empowered with weapon-mantras over that whole direction, showing his skill in shooting at sound."}},{"n":29,"text":"कर्णिनालीकनाराचानुत्सृजन्भरतर्षभ ।\nअनेकैरिषुसंघातैरन्तरिक्षं ववर्ष ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Releasing barbed shafts, arrows and iron shafts, best of Bharatas, he rained countless volleys of arrows into the sky."}},{"text":"यक्ष उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The Yaksha said:"}},{"n":30,"text":"किं विघातेन ते पार्थ प्रश्नानुक्त्वा ततः पिब ।\nअनुक्त्वा तु ततः प्रश्नान्पीत्वैव न भविष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"What use is this obstruction to you, Partha? Answer my questions, then drink. If you drink without answering the questions, you will not live."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":31,"text":"स त्वमोघानिषून्मुक्त्वा तृष्णयाभिप्रपीडितः ।\nअविज्ञायैव तान्प्रश्नान्पीत्वैव निपपात ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"He, having shot his arrows in vain and oppressed by thirst, without understanding the questions, drank, and as he drank, he fell."}},{"n":32,"text":"अथाब्रवीद्भीमसेनं कुन्तीपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nनकुलः सहदेवश्च बीभत्सुश्चापराजितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Yudhishthira son of Kunti said to Bhimasena: Nakula, Sahadeva, and the unconquered Bibhatsu,"}},{"n":33,"text":"चिरं गतास्तोयहेतोर्न चागच्छन्ति भारत ।\nतांश्चैवानय भद्रं ते पानीयं च त्वमानय ॥","meaning":{"en":"have been gone long for water and do not return, Bharata. Good fortune to you; bring them back and bring water too."}},{"n":34,"text":"भीमसेनस्तथेत्युक्त्वा तां दिशं प्रत्यपद्यत ।\nयत्र ते पुरुषव्याघ्रा भ्रातरोऽस्य निपातिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena said, So be it, and went in that direction, where those tigers among men, his brothers, had fallen."}},{"n":35,"text":"तान्दृष्ट्वा दुःखितो भीमस्तृषया च प्रपीडितः ।\nअमन्यत महाबाहुः कर्म तद्यक्षरक्षसाम् ।\nस चिन्तयामास तदा योद्धव्यं ध्रुवमद्य मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing them, Bhima was grieved and oppressed by thirst. The mighty-armed one thought this was the work of Yakshas and Rakshasas, and he thought: today I surely must fight."}},{"n":36,"text":"पास्यामि तावत्पानीयमिति पार्थो वृकोदरः ।\nततोऽभ्यधावत्पानीयं पिपासुः पुरुषर्षभः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Partha Vrikodara, best of men, thought: first I will drink water; and thirsty he ran to the water."}},{"text":"यक्ष उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The Yaksha said:"}},{"n":37,"text":"मा तात साहसं कार्षीर्मम पूर्वपरिग्रहः ।\nप्रश्नानुक्त्वा तु कौन्तेय ततः पिब हरस्व च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Do not act rashly, dear child; this is my prior possession. Answer my questions first, son of Kunti, then drink and take water."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":38,"text":"एवमुक्तस्ततो भीमो यक्षेणामिततेजसा ।\nअविज्ञायैव तान्प्रश्नान्पीत्वैव निपपात ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed by the Yaksha of immeasurable might, Bhima, without understanding the questions, drank, and as he drank he fell."}},{"n":39,"text":"ततः कुन्तीसुतो राजा विचिन्त्य पुरुषर्षभः ।\nसमुत्थाय महाबाहुर्दह्यमानेन चेतसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the king, son of Kunti, best of men, thinking it over, rose, his mind burning with anxiety, mighty-armed."}},{"n":40,"text":"अपेतजननिर्घोषं प्रविवेश महावनम् ।\nरुरुभिश्च वराहैश्च पक्षिभिश्च निषेवितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He entered the great forest, empty of human sounds, frequented by ruru deer, boars and birds."}},{"n":41,"text":"नीलभास्वरवर्णैश्च पादपैरुपशोभितम् ।\nभ्रमरैरुपगीतं च पक्षिभिश्च महायशाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was adorned with trees of dark, shining color, and sung to by bees and birds, of great renown."}},{"n":42,"text":"स गच्छन्कानने तस्मिन्हेमजालपरिष्कृतम् ।\nददर्श तत्सरः श्रीमान्विश्वकर्मकृतं यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going through that forest, the glorious one saw a lake adorned with golden nets, as if made by Vishvakarman."}},{"n":43,"text":"उपेतं नलिनीजालैः सिन्धुवारैश्च वेतसैः ।\nकेतकैः करवीरैश्च पिप्पलैश्चैव संवृतम् ।\nश्रमार्तस्तदुपागम्य सरो दृष्ट्वाथ विस्मितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was filled with lotus clusters, and surrounded by sindhuvara, cane, ketaka, karavira and pippala trees. Weary, he came to that lake and saw it with amazement."}}]}]}